#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Pegasus Bridge: Normandy, 6 June 1944.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Ten minutes after midnight on D-Day, three gliders land beside the
bridge over the Caen Canal at Bénouville and two more by the bridge
over the Orne.  D Company of the Ox and Bucks takes both in a few
minutes.  Now it must hold them, through the night and the morning,
until the commandos come up from Sword Beach.  Play either side against
the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./pegasus (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.pegasus.json.  ./pegasus --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

